## DESCRIPTION
## DBsubject(Statistics)
## DBchapter(Exploratory data analysis/descriptive statistics)
## DBsection(Summary statistics)
## Institution(The College of Idaho)
## Author(R Cruz, L Danielson, J Guild)
## MLT(stat-des-mean-stdev)
## Level(1)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('The Basic Practice of Statistics')
## AuthorText1('David Moore')
## EditionText1('5e')
## Section1('2')
## Problem1('')
## KEYWORDS('statistics', 'mean', 'variance', 'standard deviation')

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGstatisticsmacros.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

@a = map { random(5, 50) } (1 .. 9);

$mean     = stats_mean(@a);
$sd       = stats_sd(@a);
$variance = $sd**2;
$range    = max(@a) - min(@a);

BEGIN_PGML
Given the data set below, calculate the range, mean, sample variance, and sample standard deviation.

[```  [@ join(', ', @a) @] ```] 

a) Range [`=`] [_]{$range}

b) Mean [`=`] [_]{$mean}

c) Variance [`=`] [_]{$variance}

d) Standard deviation [`=`] [_]{$sd}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a) the range is the difference of the largest value, [@max(@a)@] and the smallest [@ min(@a) @] or range = [$range]

b) The mean is the sum of the values over the number of values or 

    [```\bar{x} = \frac{[@ join('+',@a) @]}{[@scalar(@a) @]} = [@ Round($mean,3) @] ```]

c) The variable is found with the formula

    [``` 
    \begin{aligned}
    s^2 & = \frac{(x_1-\bar{x})^2 + (x_2-\bar{x})^2 + \cdot (x_n-\bar{x})^2 }{n-1} \\
    & = \frac{ ([$a[0]]-[@ Round($mean,3) @])^2 + ([$a[1]]-[@ Round($mean,3) @])^2 + \cdots + ([$a[8]]-[@ Round($mean,3) @])^2}{7} = [@ Round($variance,3) @] 
    \end{aligned}
    ```]

    Alternatively, one can use the formula

    [``` \begin{aligned}
    s^2 & = \frac{x_1^2 + x_2^2 + \cdots + x_n^2}{n} - \frac{n}{n-1} (\bar{x})^2 \\
     & = \frac{[$a[0]]^2 + [$a[1]]^2 + \cdots + [$a[8]]^2}{8- 9/8*(26.2222^2)} - \frac{9}{8} ([$mean])^2 \\
     & = [$variance]
    \end{aligned}```]

d) The standard deviation is the square root of the variance or 

    [``` s = \sqrt{[$variance]} = [@Round($sd,3)@] ```]
    
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();       # This should be the last executable line in the problem.